  "name": "Venomancer: Tranquil Essence, Soothing Venoms and Spirit of the Jungle modifiers (#978, #1048, #1084)",
  "contract": "#978 Tranquil Essence (504799 rank 1, 505204 rank 2): two SPELL_AURA_ADD_PCT_MODIFIER (108) effects, EffectMiscValue 2 (SPELLMOD_THREAT, BasePoints -11/-21 + die 1 = -10/-20) and 22 (SPELLMOD_DOT, 2/5 + 1 = +3/+6), class mask (0x80801, 0x8008000, 0x80000) selecting Shadra's Balm (800901, word0 0x800) and the Rejuvenating Venom heal (630869, words 1 and 2). ThreatManager.cpp applies SPELLMOD_THREAT and Unit::SpellHealingBonusDone applies SPELLMOD_DOT for periodic healing, both through Player::ApplySpellMod, so spell_modifier reads exactly what a cast uses. Base 1000 gives 900/800 for threat and 1030/1060 for DoT (percent DoT modifiers are multiplicative, ApplySpellMod). #1048 Soothing Venoms (707726, 707869): aura 108 with misc 15 (SPELLMOD_CRIT_DAMAGE_BONUS), 24/49 + 1 = +25/+50, mask (0, 0x8000000, 0x40000) selecting Shadra's Prayer (800870) and Emerald Veil (800926); Unit::SpellCriticalHealingBonus applies the modifier to the crit bonus at Unit.cpp:9993. The harness has no critical-healing metric, so the modifier itself is asserted (1000 -> 1250/1500). #1084 Spirit of the Jungle (681048): aura 107 (flat) misc 18 (SPELLMOD_CHANCE_OF_SUCCESS), 9 + 1 = +10, mask word1 0x400 selecting the Rejuvenating Venom activation 630868, whose spell_proc row has Chance 0 so SpellMgr.cpp uses Spell.dbc ProcChance 20; Aura::CalcProcChance then applies the modifier (SpellAuras.cpp:2313) for 30%. The proc rate itself is statistical and is not sampled here; the modifier on the base chance is. Ranks 1 and 2 are fixtured on separate actors so the modifiers do not stack. Controls: Hivebreak and Shadra's Balm/Prayer outside each mask, and an unlearned actor.",
